title dexter shell -- the prompt session, line married to history, GREEN
prompt autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, send often, stop at custody gates
think The editable line (dexter_line) and its history ring (dexter_history) both stand GREEN and sent. The honest next crux is the prompt state machine that weds them -- the session a keeper actually drives: type, submit (remember and clear), and walk history with up/down, recalling a committed line INTO the editable line. Pure composition over both modules' public APIs, ungated, finishable green in one lap.
think Built pond/apps/dexter_shell.rye: a Prompt holding a Line, a History, and a stashed draft. submit commits the line to history and clears it; up recalls the previous committed line into the line (stashing the in-progress draft on the first step up from the live edge); down recalls the next, and stepping off the newest restores the stashed draft. Past the oldest refuses NoEarlier, past the live edge NoLater -- both bubbling up from the ring unchanged.
think The draft stash is the completeness the SLC lens asks for: a prompt that ate your half-typed line on up-arrow would be unlovable. Stepping up from the live edge saves the line; stepping back down restores it exactly. load_line replaces the editable line's contents via public insert, so a recalled line arrives editable with the cursor at the end.
obs GREEN on the first metal run -- no red at all this lap. tame_style_check bans clean (no compound asserts), width-check exit 0, new prose plain ASCII, American spelling. The witness build compiled the unchanged dexter_line and dexter_history, so both prior rungs stand intact -- composition, not modification.
obs This ties to the grain (rota item 24): values apart, never braided. dexter_shell composes two whole modules through their public APIs, braiding neither -- a value crosses the boundary whole. The prompt is one bounded entry gathering the pieces beneath it, the quin_host shape carried to the terminal.
obs Rota lap (d27, item 24) read active-designing/20260702-184312_the-grain-and-the-crossing.md -- the grain is the standing commitments a new idea must be cut to fit; composition over tangling is one strand, and this rung leans only on it.
loom witness=dexter_shell_witness selftest=GREEN selftest_cases=4 composes=dexter_line+dexter_history
